<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KR">Corollary <span data-tag="01KR">4.6.4.14</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing an object $X$, and let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. Then the projection map $\{ X\}  \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a left fibration, and the projection map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \{ X\}  \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a right fibration. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Unwinding the definition, we have pullback diagrams 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \{ X\}  \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \{ X\}  \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \{ X\}  \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \{ X\}  \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{F} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}&amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{F} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}. } \]
</div>
<p>
       The desired result now follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="01KQ" href="/tag/01KQ">4.6.4.13</a> with Remark <a data-tag="014N" href="/tag/014N">4.2.1.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
